cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Adolescent ball-sport finger fractures and dislocations: reproducible NEISS analysis pipeline, 2015-2025"
abstract: >-
  A fully reproducible analysis pipeline for national emergency department estimates of
  adolescent finger fractures and dislocations associated with selected ball sports, using
  public CPSC National Electronic Injury Surveillance System (NEISS) annual archived data
  for treatment years 2015-2025. The pipeline downloads the official source files, verifies
  product/activity code mappings against the official CPSC data dictionary, constructs the
  analytic cohort, and produces all tables, figures and supplementary material reported in
  the associated manuscript, including survey-weighted national estimates with design-based
  confidence intervals, a survey-weighted temporal analysis, and the adjusted case-mix model.
type: software
